# Ward / nursing UX

Ward owns **ward and nursing operational workflow**: ward board, bed map, patient status, nursing tasks, checklist/medication/vitals capture already in this kit, pre-op readiness, post-op care, transfer, discharge readiness, ward dashboards.

Canonical page: `/dashboard/ip-management/ward`. Canonical components: `WardBedMap`, `WardKpiStrip`, `WardChecklist*`, `WardPatientDrawer`, `WardPreOp/PostOp/DischargeWorkspaceModal`, step navs, gate chips. Stay inside `IpTargetFrame` and `IpOverlayDialog`.

Ward is **not** a separate app. Reuse `components/ip-management`. Do not create `components/ward` unless explicitly approved.

## Usability

Prioritize high-frequency desktop use (nurses, ward clerks). Keep primary actions reachable without hunting. Preserve existing testids used by Playwright ward-journey specs. Do not densify for decoration.

## Boundaries

- Clinical chart/EHR remains patient record / doctor desk / examination — ward workspaces collect operational/clinical checklist data in the IP journey, not a second EHR.
- Billing/coverage indicators may display as projections; collection still goes through Billing APIs.
- Do not duplicate OT surgical state here.
- Permissions such as `ward.checklist.edit` are server-enforced; do not expose actions on nav alone.

## Do not clone

Do not extend `module3/counselor` pre-op checklists or widgets as the ward kit. Do not add a second readiness-meter primitive if `WardReadinessMeter` / `preop/primitives/ReadinessMeter` already covers the case — reuse or compose.
